# Claude Code driving the cell over MCP (xetal-cell-mcp, its tools
# only), given mcp/goals/lap.goal: U1 in the vise legs up, then R1.1 to
# pin 8 and R2.2 to pin 6 with lap joints, without the planner. Its
# session as the server saved it (2026-11-27: 25 turns, 254 s; 15
# cell_attempt calls, 3 kept, 12 refused or stopped and left nothing
# behind); both joints good, 3.7 mm laps. Run again: just ext cell
# agent lap. What it said got in its way is on the extension's page.
reset circuit=blinker
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-32 rpy=180,0,0
vise close
release A U1
lift A mm=60
move A to=150,120,-60 rpy=180,0,90
pick A R1 grasp=body
insert A on=R1.1 at=3
form angle=90
shear A on=R1.1 at=8
bring A R1.1 to=U1.8.tip along=0,-1,0 from=0,0,1 lap=3.4
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=2
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.8+R1.1 at=S1
touch S1 at=U1.8+R1.1
feed S1 mm=3
back S1
unpinch P1
stage to=0 tilt=0 at=0,0,0
move A to=150,120,-60 rpy=180,0,90
pick A R2 grasp=body
insert A on=R2.2 at=3
form angle=90
shear A on=R2.2 at=8
bring A R2.2 to=U1.6.tip along=0,-1,0 from=0,0,1 lap=3.4
pinch P2 on=R2.2 at=2
release A R2
lift A mm=60
present U1.6+R2.2 at=S1
touch S1 at=U1.6+R2.2
feed S1 mm=3
back S1
unpinch P2
inspect U1.8+R1.1
inspect U1.6+R2.2
check
